  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: MISOGYNY; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman sitting on the edge of a bed with a distressed or weary expression, arms crossed over her chest. The text overlay reads: 'all men are dogs.. so which breed is your dad?'. This meme uses a misogynistic trope by generalizing all men as 'dogs' — a degrading metaphor implying men are inherently animalistic, untrustworthy, or lacking in moral character. The question 'so which breed is your dad?' escalates the insult by implying the father (a man) is a specific, undesirable type of dog, reinforcing the dehumanizing and derogatory stereotype. The visual of the woman looking downcast or defeated is used to imply she is suffering from this generalized male behavior, which is a classic misogynistic framing that blames women's emotional state on men's supposed inherent flaws. The overall intent is to demean men and perpetuate the idea that men are inherently flawed or animal-like, which is a form of misogynistic humor that reinforces harmful gender stereotypes and can contribute to a culture of resentment or hostility toward men, while also potentially validating the emotional distress of the woman depicted as a consequence of male behavior.",
